Subject: Hide "Get New Pages…" when KNewStuff is not allowed

With [KDE Action Restrictions] ghns=false, NewStuff.Action disables and
hides itself, but two entries that open it do not follow: the File menu's
Labs.MenuItem calls showHotNewStuff() directly and stays visible, doing
nothing when clicked, and the sidebar's context menu item shows the action
greyed out. Both now take the visibility KNewStuff's own kiosk check gives,
and the context menu item collapses to no height while hidden, as an
invisible item in a QtQuick.Controls Menu otherwise keeps its row.

--- a/src/GlobalMenu.qml
+++ b/src/GlobalMenu.qml
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
         Labs.MenuItem {
             text: i18nc("@menu-action", "Get New Pages…")
             icon.name: "get-hot-new-stuff"
+            visible: NewStuff.Settings.allowedByKiosk
             onTriggered: ghnsAction.showHotNewStuff()
         }
 
--- a/src/Main.qml
+++ b/src/Main.qml
@@ -253,7 +253,11 @@
                 id: globalContextMenu
 
                 MenuItem { action: editPagesAction }
-                MenuItem { action: ghnsAction }
+                MenuItem {
+                    action: ghnsAction
+                    visible: ghnsAction.visible
+                    height: visible ? implicitHeight : 0
+                }
                 MenuItem { action: collapseAction }
             }
         ]
